# Tailwind CSS v4 in this project

This project uses Tailwind **v4** with the `@tailwindcss/vite` plugin.
The setup is CSS-first. Do NOT generate Tailwind v3 patterns.

## Do

- Configure Tailwind via `src/index.css` only:

```css
@import "tailwindcss";

/* Custom tokens (optional) */
@theme {
  --color-brand: oklch(0.72 0.18 155);
  --font-display: "Inter", sans-serif;
}
```

- Register the plugin in `vite.config.ts`:

```ts
import tailwindcss from "@tailwindcss/vite";
plugins: [react(), tailwindcss()];
```

- Use the standard utility class API on JSX (`<div className="p-4 text-emerald-600" />`).

## Don't

- Don't create `tailwind.config.ts` / `tailwind.config.js`. v4 ignores it.
- Don't write `@tailwind base; @tailwind components; @tailwind utilities;`.
  Use `@import "tailwindcss";` instead.
- Don't add a `postcss.config.*` file. v4 uses the Vite plugin directly.
- Don't add `@apply` in shared component CSS unless inside a `@layer`
  block in `src/index.css` — colocated `className` is the preferred style.
- Don't `npm install tailwindcss@3` or `autoprefixer` / `postcss` as Tailwind deps.

## Reference

- v4 docs: https://tailwindcss.com/docs/installation/using-vite
